Grade /root/bench-runs/h4-b3949ce2/server.mjs (new file, all lines changed) and /root/bench-runs/h4-b3949ce2/package.json. The spec is /root/bench-runs/h4-b3949ce2/.team/notes/spec.md, sections "Server", "API", "Booking rules" and the first bullet of "Page". Check every spec line in those sections against the code for correctness: exact statuses, messages and content-types; the rule order 415, 413, 400s, 409; byte-for-byte path matching; PORT parsing; data-file load and validation; save before reply, with no change on failure; serialized concurrency; reading the whole body before replying; never crashing on a request.

This is fix round 1. Last round scored 8 and gave these fixes:
- split the 130-line createApp: now createRepository plus module-level handlers;
- one-line stderr for a bad PORT;
- a lasting server 'error' handler after listen;
- a shared comparer for the 409 sort;
- removed the redundant typeof checks.

The temp-file + rename fix was deliberately NOT applied. Keeping plain writeFile is the supervisor's explicit job decision. Rename would also quietly replace a read-only data file, which turns a save that should fail into a success. The trade-off (a write that fails partway could damage the file) is logged in /root/bench-runs/h4-b3949ce2/.team/notes/decisions.md. Do not deduct for it unless you see a spec violation beyond that accepted trade-off.

Constraints: Node.js built-ins only. House rules:
- return new objects instead of mutating;
- functions under 50 lines, files at most 800 lines;
- validate input at boundaries;
- handle errors explicitly and never swallow them;
- user-facing errors friendly and leaking nothing;
- no console.log and no hardcoded secrets.

Tests: the testing section writes them, so score tests n/a and leave them out of the overall. The smoke script /root/bench-runs/h4-b3949ce2/.team/scratch/smoke.mjs is not graded. You may run `node /root/bench-runs/h4-b3949ce2/.team/scratch/smoke.mjs` (it prints ALL OK).

Pass bar: overall >= 9 and no item < 7. Give a file:line fix list and end with your GRADE block.

